{
  "title": "Intel post-2030 joint operating scenarios: policy frozen before new scenario equity outputs",
  "frozen_utc": "2026-11-04T18:07:07.495010+00:00",
  "owner": "operating_scenario_policy",
  "scope": "A bounded challenge to the current ASP20/mature35 host. Preserve the already funded 2027-2030 operating/treasury path and the separate packaging program. These are conditional continuation scenarios, not a complete probability-weighted forecast or a newly chosen stock direction.",
  "chronology": "Historical and current central valuations, including the recent discount-rate diagnostic, are known from inherited context. No new equity value or joint scenario output has been computed or inspected in selecting this policy.",
  "root_choice_recommendation": "Retain the existing 35% DCAI margin/0.80 capital-productivity central forecast for this pass. Compare it with 30%/0.60 and 40%/1.00 coherent continuation cases; do not relabel the high case as central solely because its value reaches a desired price.",
  "why_these_ranges": {
    "DCAI_margin": "30-40% brackets plausible normalization of the current roughly 42% segment margin and uncertainty about CPU pricing, product development scale and lower-margin custom mix. At the modelled mature Other DCAI share of about one quarter, 40% requires strong CPU profitability; it is a favorable outcome, not a neutral assumption. Existing primary-history scopes differ, so neither old peak margins nor one scarcity quarter establish a steady-state floor.",
    "capital_productivity": "0.60-1.00 spans the prior same-company flow diagnostic and a meaningful further improvement from paid factory space and longer node use. 0.80 remains a reasonable planning middle. The endpoints are economic judgments, not measured marginal-capital coefficients, physical bounds, percentiles or statistical confidence intervals.",
    "joint_logic": "The two dimensions represent different mechanisms: product economic rent/cost leverage affects DCAI margin; physical capacity required per incremental sale affects capital. Pairing them in favorable and unfavorable directions is an internally consistent business narrative, not an estimated correlation."
  },
  "implementation": {
    "current_value_source": "/Users/thomasou/Documents/Codex/2026-11-02/lo/work/three_hour/active_research/pricing_and_competition_review_2026_11_04/intel_ASP20_mature_margin35_valuation.json",
    "host_policy": "/Users/thomasou/Documents/Codex/2026-11-02/lo/work/three_hour/active_research/pricing_and_competition_review_2026_11_04/intel_server_ASP_mix_operating_policy.json",
    "margin_policy": "/Users/thomasou/Documents/Codex/2026-11-02/lo/work/three_hour/active_research/pricing_and_competition_review_2026_11_04/intel_mature_DCAI_margin_addendum.json",
    "margin_rule": "For year y >2030, DCAI margin = current35-policy margin + (target-.35)*min((y-2030)/10,1). Multiply the delta by unchanged DCAI sales and add once to group EBIT. This reaches 30/35/40% in2040. Do not add a second manufacturing saving to Foundry.",
    "capital_rule": "For year y >2030, host turnover = .80 + (target-.80)*min((y-2030)/5,1), reaching .60/.80/1.00 in2035. Gross physical host capex = unchanged normalized host DA + change in host external-sales denominator / turnover - unchanged host WC cash use. This changes investment for new growth; it does not retroactively release or recover already-spent capital.",
    "combined_model_delta": "Add DCAI revenue times margin delta to current combined EBIT. Add host external-sales change*(1/turnover-1/.8) to current combined physical capex. All package, tax-credit, lease, NCI, recurring economic SBC and claims assumptions are unchanged. Recompute ordinary operating taxes on changed EBIT and verify any tax-capacity assumptions; do not leave taxes unchanged mechanically.",
    "near_term_and_endpoints": "All2027-2030 rows are unchanged, so end2026 through end2030 treasury/cash/debt remain unchanged. Endpoint operating values still change because they discount later cash. If reporting2031 or later equity endpoints, recompute retained cash/treasury, including the changed operating cash, once.",
    "terminal": "Hold target margin and turnover after2040. Preserve3% nominal growth, separately funded packaging and its1.00 turnover. Verify that2041 terminal operating cash grows consistently from2040; never apply host turnover to packaging sales a second time.",
    "depreciation_scope": "Preserve the aggregate normalized DA path (20% of Products by2035) and margins defined after that depreciation. This is an aggregate economic forecast, not a vintaged PP&E/tax-depreciation reconstruction. Higher or lower future physical capital and chosen profit margins must be understood jointly; no claim that unchanged accounting DA is mechanically exact for changed asset cohorts.",
    "no_new_funding_credit": "No extra AMIC, customer funding, external wafer award, partner cash or minority ownership adjustment is invented. Their economics require a separate evidence-based model if added."
  },
  "risk_context": {
    "preferred_reporting": "Show the same common discount-rate columns for every operating case so the operational result is separated from the risk-rate judgment. Keep the already selected12% as the central comparison and retain10/11/13% diagnostics if root uses them. Do not silently pair the favorable case only with10% and the unfavorable case only with13%.",
    "interpretation": "Successful execution can reduce uncertainty, but lower uncertainty is not a measured lower systematic asset beta. A mature leading-edge manufacturer still faces pricing, demand, technology and capital cycles. The existing sector-based12% rationale is imperfect but not arbitrary. A lower rate is a separate hypothesis to defend rather than a reward automatically attached to high margins.",
    "optional_separate_test": "If root tests de-risking after the investment phase, explicitly distinguish a future lower continuation discount rate from discounting every near-term cash flow at that lower rate today; do not count de-risking as both better cash and an unexplained re-rating."
