      ],
      "facts": "Intel aims to extend process-node use through optimization, disaggregated products and external customers. Its 2025 net PP&E was $105.414B, including $34.543B construction in progress. It also recorded manufacturing impairments and accelerated depreciation after reuse assessments.",
      "inference": "Prebuilt space and node reuse support improvement, but substantial unfinished capacity is neither immediately productive nor freely reusable. Recent impairment experience prevents treating all old capacity as an economic asset forever."
    },
    {
      "id": "intel_q3_2026_remarks",
